          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em conformal structure
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            is the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} Riemannian metric
            modulo rescalings of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+metric"} metric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor"} tensor
            by some real valued function on the manifold. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            of conformal structures are called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+transformations"} conformal transformations
          %p
            In terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            conformal structure is expressed by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+connections"} conformal connections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parabolic+geometry"} parabolic geometry
            and hence of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            conformal structure underlies the formulation of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+group"} conformal group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+group"} anti de Sitter group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti+de+Sitter+spacetime"} anti de Sitter spacetime
            in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d+1
            there is a close relation between certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theories"} conformal field theories
            and certain theories of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS-CFT+correspondence"} AdS-CFT correspondence
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superconformal+groups"} superconformal groups
            acting on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/asymptotic+boundary"} asymptotic boundary
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+anti+de+Sitter+spacetimes"} super anti de Sitter spacetimes
